&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="tick-labels-keep-matplotlibs-look"&gt;Tick labels keep matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s look&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="tick-labels-keep-matplotlibs-look"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#tick-labels-keep-matplotlibs-look" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The one exception is &lt;code&gt;\mathdefault{...}&lt;/code&gt;, which is what matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s tick
formatters emit (&lt;code&gt;10^{3}&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;2\times10^{1}&lt;/code&gt;). It is set in &lt;strong&gt;DejaVu Sans&lt;/strong&gt; with
mathtext&amp;rsquo;s own superscript rules (shift = max(sup1 · x-height, depth +
x-height/4), scripts at 0.7 size), so tick labels match matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s look and
position. The decades on the &lt;a href="https://go-plot.github.io/docs/0.3/plot-types/#log-scales"&gt;log-log figure&lt;/a&gt;
are set this way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="plain-text"&gt;Plain text&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="plain-text"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#plain-text" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Text outside dollar signs is set in &lt;strong&gt;DejaVu Sans&lt;/strong&gt;, matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s default
font, from go-opentype/fonts, with kerning from DejaVu&amp;rsquo;s GPOS and kern tables.
Glyphs are drawn as filled outlines, so rotated labels and SVG output need no
font. Positions follow matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;Text._get_layout&lt;/code&gt; (line metrics from the
OS/2 table, alignment, rotation, anchoring), and like Agg the pen is put on a
whole pixel. How the pixels of text differ from matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s is on
&lt;a href="https://go-plot.github.io/docs/0.3/differences/#text"&gt;Differences&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="text-from-data-no-tex"&gt;Text from data: no TeX&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="text-from-data-no-tex"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#text-from-data-no-tex" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A string is read as matplotlib reads it: TeX between an even number of
unescaped dollar signs. Names that come from data (&amp;ldquo;100$&amp;rdquo;, a team called
&lt;code&gt;$x$&lt;/code&gt;) should not be. go-plot follows matplotlib&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;parse_math&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;go-plot&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;matplotlib&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;plot.NewFigure(plot.ParseMath(false))&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fig.SetParseMath(false)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;rcParams[&amp;quot;text.parse_math&amp;quot;] = False&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;plot.PlainText()&lt;/code&gt; on one call&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;parse_math=False&lt;/code&gt; on that text&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;plot.MathText()&lt;/code&gt; on one call&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;parse_math=True&lt;/code&gt; on that text&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The calls that take it are &lt;code&gt;SetTitle&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;SetXLabel&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;SetYLabel&lt;/code&gt;. So do
&lt;code&gt;SetXTickLabels&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;SetYTickLabels&lt;/code&gt; (category names under bars), &lt;code&gt;Legend&lt;/code&gt;
(every entry), &lt;code&gt;Text&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Annotate&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Pie&lt;/code&gt;. A plain string is drawn
character for character as glyph outlines. It never reaches the TeX
typesetter, and &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; becomes shapes, not markup. The tick labels
go-plot&amp;rsquo;s formatters write (&lt;code&gt;10³&lt;/code&gt; on a log axis) stay math.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="cost"&gt;Cost&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="cost"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#cost" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;STIX Two Math is parsed only when a label contains TeX: a figure without any
does not pay for it (&lt;a href="https://go-plot.github.io/docs/0.3/performance/"&gt;performance&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="replacing-the-renderer"&gt;Replacing the renderer&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="replacing-the-renderer"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#replacing-the-renderer" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Figure.Text&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;code&gt;text.Renderer&lt;/code&gt; with two methods, &lt;code&gt;Layout(s, size)&lt;/code&gt; and
&lt;code&gt;LineMetrics(size)&lt;/code&gt;. Setting another one changes the fonts of the whole figure.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>